{
  "sources": {
    "ignore": ["/solid-2"]
  },
  "families": [
    {
      "id": "worktrees",
      "title": "Worktrees & branches",
      "icon": "code branch",
      "intro": "Git worktrees under `.claude/worktrees/<name>`, one branch each:  made, checked, merged, removed.  Mostly skill prose today.",
      "rows": [
        {
          "op": "Create or enter a worktree",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "could",
            "note": "`epic worktree new <name>`;  Claude still needs `EnterWorktree` to move the session"
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "other",
            "names": ["/isolate", "/epic", "/park", "/unpark", "/bedtime"],
            "note": "`EnterWorktree`;  `/bedtime` only via isolate"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "could",
            "note": "from the main checkout only"
          },
          "runs": "`EnterWorktree` -> `.claude/hooks/worktree.mjs create`",
          "notes": "Hook branches from LOCAL `main`, names branch `<name>` (Claude's own adds `worktree-`), reuses an existing worktree / branch.",
          "target": "(R3) `epic worktree new <name>`;  Claude still moves the session with `EnterWorktree`"
        },
        {
          "op": "Lower-kebab-case a name",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "could"
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "other",
            "names": ["/isolate", "/epic", "/park"],
            "note": "prose"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "could"
          },
          "runs": "skill prose;  the `epic` tool (`PlanDocFiles`) only rejects non-kebab names",
          "notes": "Fourth layer.  `worktree.mjs` allows `[A-Za-z0-9._-]`:  looser than the skills' rule.",
          "target": "(R3) `epic worktree name-check <name>` kebab-cases;  hook `worktree.mjs` shares the rule"
        },
        {
          "op": "Check a worktree name is free",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "could",
            "note": "`spell dev name-free <name>`:  worktree, branch, `worktree-<name>`, epic page"
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "other",
            "names": ["/isolate", "/epic"],
            "note": "`/epic` adds epic-page paths"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "could"
          },
          "runs": "`git worktree list`, `git branch` + prose",
          "notes": "Fourth layer, duplicated in two skills.  Hit:  modal \"Reuse\" / \"Different name\".",
          "target": "(R3) `epic worktree name-check <name> --json`:  worktree, branch, epic page;  /isolate /epic call it"
        },
        {
          "op": "Carry uncommitted edits into a new worktree",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "could",
            "note": "mechanics only;  which files are whose needs Claude"
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "other",
            "names": ["/isolate", "/park"],
            "note": "`/isolate` asks first;  `/park` carries this session's files only"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "could",
            "note": "mechanics only"
          },
          "runs": "`git stash` + prose",
          "notes": "Bare `git stash pop` in both skills:  can pop another session's stash (shared stack).  `/park` pushes `-m park:<name>` but still pops bare.",
          "target": "(R3) `epic worktree carry <name> <files>`:  tagged stash, applied by sha;  skill picks files"
        },
        {
          "op": "Install dependencies if missing",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "could",
            "note": "`spell` itself needs the main checkout's `node_modules`"
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "other",
            "names": ["/isolate", "/epic", "/unpark", "/wait-for"],
            "note": "`/isolate` step 7, park Resume step 3"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "no",
            "note": "yarn runs no script in a worktree before `yarn install`"
          },
          "runs": "`yarn install` + prose",
          "notes": "Resume also reinstalls when `yarn.lock` or workspaces changed in the merge.",
          "target": "(R3) `epic worktree new` / `merge-main` run `yarn install` when missing or lockfile changed"
        },
        {
          "op": "Report uncommitted and unmerged work",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "could",
            "note": "`epic worktree status`"
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "other",
            "names": ["/isolate", "/worktrees", "/wtf"],
            "note": "`/isolate done` step 1"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "could"
          },
          "runs": "`git status --short`, `git log main..HEAD`;  `epic update`, `epic worktree status` (`ahead`)",
          "notes": "Three implementations:  skill prose, `epic update`, `epic worktree status`.",
          "target": "(R3) `epic worktree status [name] --json`;  /isolate /worktrees /wtf call it"
        },
        {
          "op": "Check a branch merges cleanly",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "could",
            "note": "`git merge-tree` exit code, conflicting files"
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "other",
            "names": ["/isolate", "/worktrees", "/unpark", "/wait-for"],
            "note": "`/isolate done` step 2, park Resume step 2"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "could"
          },
          "runs": "`git merge-tree --write-tree --name-only main HEAD` + prose",
          "notes": "Fourth layer, copied into `/isolate`, `/park` Resume, `/worktrees` merge.",
          "target": "(R3) `epic worktree merge-check <name> --json`;  /isolate /unpark /wait-for /worktrees call it"
        },
        {
          "op": "Merge main into a worktree",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "other",
            "names": ["epic worktree"],
            "note": "`merge-main [--continue]`:  regenerates generated files both sides changed (bundles, snapshots);  other conflicts stop it for Claude"
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "other",
            "names": ["/isolate", "/unpark", "/wait-for"],
            "note": "other conflicts resolved keeping both sides' intent, then `merge-main --continue`"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "could",
            "note": "clean merges only"
          },
          "runs": "`epic worktree merge-main` (`packages/cli/src/dev/mergeMain.ts`, `GENERATORS`)",
          "notes": "Generated files are `merge=binary` in the root `.gitattributes`:  never line-merged, regenerated from the merged source;  a snapshot entry neither side had is reported for review.  Package moves on `main` show as rename / delete conflicts:  park Resume says follow the move and fix aliases.",
          "target": "(R3) built:  `epic worktree merge-main`;  `/isolate` and park Resume (`/unpark`, `/wait-for`) call it"
        },
        {
          "op": "Run checks for the packages a branch touches",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "could",
            "note": "`spell dev check --touched`;  `spell lint` checks spell projects, not packages"
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "other",
            "names": ["/unpark", "/wait-for", "/isolate", "/bedtime"],
            "note": "park Resume step 3"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "could",
            "note": "root `ts` / `test` run EVERY package;  no touched-only script"
          },
          "runs": "`git diff --name-only main...HEAD` -> `yarn ts`, `yarn test` per package",
          "notes": "Fourth layer.",
          "target": "(R7) `spell dev check --touched`;  park Resume, /isolate, /bedtime call it"
        },
        {
          "op": "Merge a worktree into main",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "could",
            "note": "`epic worktree merge <name>`"
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "other",
            "names": ["/isolate", "/worktrees"],
            "note": "`/isolate done`;  `/wakeup` runs its steps"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "could"
          },
          "runs": "`git merge --ff-only <name>` (`/isolate`) or `git merge --no-edit <branch>` (`epic update`)",
          "notes": "DRIFT:  `/isolate` fast-forwards only;  `epic update` makes a merge commit, while its docstring says \"as `/isolate done` would\".",
          "target": "(R3) `epic worktree merge <name>`:  ONE policy;  /isolate /worktrees call it"
        },
        {
          "op": "Leave a worktree",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "no",
            "note": "`ExitWorktree` is Claude-only"
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "other",
            "names": ["/isolate", "/epic"],
            "note": "`/isolate done`, or `/epic done` (the same steps);  `/epic` Doc Review calls it"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "no"
          },
          "runs": "`window.mjs handoff --back`, then `ExitWorktree keep`",
          "notes": "Never `remove` unasked;  the hook's `remove` refuses without `discard_changes`.",
          "target": "stays:  Claude-only (`ExitWorktree keep`);  after (R2) `epic window handoff --back`"
        },
        {
          "op": "Remove a finished worktree and its branch",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "could",
            "note": "`epic worktree remove <name>`"
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "other",
            "names": ["/isolate", "/worktrees"],
            "note": "`/isolate done` cleanup;  `/whassup` remove"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "could"
          },
          "runs": "`git worktree remove` + `git branch -d`;  `worktree.mjs remove` hook",
          "notes": "`epic update` uses `-D` for squashed-in branches;  the skill checks `git cherry` first.",
          "target": "(R3) `epic worktree remove <name>`:  `git cherry` before `-D`;  /isolate /worktrees call it"
        },
        {
          "op": "Throw away a worktree's work",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "could",
            "note": "behind a confirm"
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "other",
            "names": ["/worktrees"],
            "note": "`discard`, asks twice"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "could"
          },
          "runs": "`git worktree remove --force`, `git branch -D` (`epic update`)",
          "target": "(R3) `epic worktree remove <name> --discard`;  /worktrees confirms twice first"
        },
        {
          "op": "Find worktrees safe to clean up",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "could",
            "note": "`epic worktree list --dead`"
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "other",
            "names": ["/isolate", "/worktrees"],
            "note": "`/isolate done` outside a worktree"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "could"
          },
          "runs": "`/isolate`:  parses `epic worktree list` TEXT + `git`;  `epic update` `dead` group",
          "notes": "Two rules for \"dead\":  `/isolate` prose vs `epic update`.",
          "target": "(R3) `epic worktree cleanup --json`:  ONE \"dead\" rule;  /isolate /worktrees call it"
        },
        {
          "op": "List worktrees and the session in each",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["epic worktree"],
            "note": "`list [--json]`"
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "other",
            "names": ["/worktrees"]
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "could"
          },
          "runs": "`packages/cli/src/dev/worktrees.ts` (`sessionPlaces()`)",
          "notes": "`/worktrees` is a user skill (`~/.claude/skills`), not in the repo.",
          "target": "(R3) built:  `epic worktree list`;  /worktrees and /isolate call it"
        },
        {
          "op": "Say where a worktree's folder is, or where a new one goes",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["epic worktree"],
            "note": "`path <name>`:  absolute;  beside the repo (`worktreesFolder`), or the old `.claude/worktrees/<name>` while one is still there"
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "other",
            "names": ["/isolate", "/epic", "/park", "/unpark", "/epics", "/wtf", "/docs-check"],
            "note": "`EnterWorktree`'s `path`, and `git -C \"$(epic worktree path <name>)\"`"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "no"
          },
          "runs": "spell-epic's `Worktrees` (`EpicConfig.worktreeFolder()`)",
          "notes": "Prints the folder even when no worktree is there yet:  where `/isolate` makes it.",
          "target": "built (epic `epic-eject` P8)"
        },
        {
          "op": "Move worktrees from the old place beside the repo",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["epic worktree"],
            "note": "`move <name> | --idle [--dry-run] [--json]`:  out of `.claude/worktrees/` into `worktreesFolder`, its shared links and session folder made again;  `--idle`:  every one no session works in"
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "no"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "no"
          },
          "runs": "spell-epic's `Worktrees` (`move()`, `moveIdle()`)",
          "notes": "A worktree a session works in stays put until its `/isolate done`;  its window file still names the old folder until reopened (`epic window open <name>`).",
          "target": "built (epic `epic-eject` P8)"
        },
        {
          "op": "Tell whether a session is in a worktree",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "could"
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "other",
            "names": ["/isolate", "/park", "/bedtime", "/unpark"],
            "note": "prose:  folder under `.claude/worktrees/`"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "could"
          },
          "runs": "skill prose;  main-root lookup duplicated in `window.mjs`, `epic session`, `epic worktree status`, `worktree.mjs`",
          "notes": "Fourth layer.",
          "target": "(R3) `epic worktree status --json` (no name:  this checkout);  one main-root lookup"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sessions",
      "title": "Sessions & windows",
      "icon": "desktop",
      "intro": "VS Code windows per package and worktree (`scripts/window.mjs`), Claude sessions, and the hooks that move and title them.",
      "rows": [
        {
          "op": "Open a worktree's own VS Code window",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["epic window"],
            "note": "passes `scripts/window.mjs` its arguments"
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "other",
            "names": ["/isolate", "/epic", "/unpark"]
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["spell-app window"],
            "note": "`open <name> [--pkg]`;  skills call `node scripts/window.mjs`"
          },
          "runs": "`scripts/window.mjs open`",
          "notes": "Skills skip `yarn window`:  a fresh worktree has no `node_modules`, and yarn runs no script there.",
          "target": "(R2) built:  `epic window open <name>`;  `node scripts/window.mjs` stays pre-install fallback"
        },
        {
          "op": "Write a worktree's window file without opening it",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["epic window"],
            "note": "`open <name> --no-open`:  the window file only, its colours already in it;  never runs `code`"
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "no"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "no"
          },
          "runs": "`src/window.mjs open` (spell-epic, `Window.open()`'s `noOpen`)",
          "notes": "For a window opened later by hand (`code <file>`, as it prints), and a check that changes nothing on the screen.",
          "target": "built (epic `epic-eject` P9)"
        },
        {
          "op": "Start an epic in a new window, from another epic's session",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["epic window"],
            "note": "`launch <name> [--color] [--prompt]`:  worktree, window, a NEW session with `/epic <name>` typed in"
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "other",
            "names": ["/epic"],
            "note": "\"From another worktree\":  the prompt hook lets `/epic <name>` through with a note;  Claude asks first"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "no"
          },
          "runs": "`scripts/window.mjs launch`",
          "target": "built (2026-10-07)"
        },
        {
          "op": "Close a worktree's window",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["epic window"]
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "other",
            "names": ["/worktrees", "/isolate"],
            "note": "`/whassup` close / remove;  `/isolate done` via `handoff --back`"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["spell-app window"],
            "note": "`close <name>`"
          },
          "runs": "`scripts/window.mjs close`",
          "target": "(R2) built:  `epic window close <name>`;  /worktrees calls it"
        },
        {
          "op": "Move a session to another window",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["epic window"],
            "note": "needs `$CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`"
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "other",
            "names": ["/isolate", "/epic", "/unpark"],
            "note": "`handoff <name>`, `--back` on leaving"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["spell-app window"],
            "note": "`handoff <name> [--back]`"
          },
          "runs": "`scripts/window.mjs handoff` -> `Stop` hook `.claude/hooks/handoff.mjs`",
          "notes": "Moves when the turn ends.  Old tab found by title:  two sessions with one title leave it open.",
          "target": "(R2) built:  `epic window handoff <name> [--back]`;  `Stop` hook `handoff.mjs` does the move"
        },
        {
          "op": "Reopen a moved session in its new window",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "no"
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "no",
            "note": "`Stop` hook only"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["spell-app window"],
            "note": "`resume <record> [--title]`, hook-only"
          },
          "runs": "`scripts/window.mjs resume`, started detached by `handoff.mjs`",
          "notes": "Log:  `~/.spell/windows/handoffs/<session id>.log`.",
          "target": "stays:  hook-only (`window.mjs resume`, started by `handoff.mjs`)"
        },
        {
          "op": "Say which window this session runs in",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["epic window"]
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "other",
            "names": ["/unpark"],
            "note": "step 3, its `workspace` line"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["spell-app window"],
            "note": "`which`"
          },
          "runs": "`scripts/window.mjs which`",
          "target": "(R2) built:  `epic window which`;  `--json` not yet;  /unpark calls it"
        },
        {
          "op": "Add or remove a folder in this window",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["epic window"]
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "other",
            "names": ["/isolate"],
            "note": "`remove`, for older sessions only"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["spell-app window"],
            "note": "`add <path>` / `remove <path>`"
          },
          "runs": "`scripts/window.mjs add|remove`",
          "notes": "Legacy:  worktrees now get their own window.",
          "target": "(R2) built:  `epic window add|remove` (passthrough);  legacy, candidate to drop"
        },
        {
          "op": "Show a doc in VS Code's doc preview",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["epic window"],
            "note": "passes `scripts/window.mjs` its arguments"
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "other",
            "names": ["/epic", "/spell-docs"],
            "note": "via `epic open`"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["spell-app window"],
            "note": "`show <file> [--review]`;  also `root epic` `open`"
          },
          "runs": "`scripts/window.mjs show` (`Window.show`), from `spell-epic/src/tools/pages.js` `openInVSCode`",
          "notes": "Waits for a pending handoff, then shows in the new window.",
          "target": "(R2) built:  `epic window show <file>`;  `epic open`, `goals open-vs` call it"
        },
        {
          "op": "Rebuild a doc view gone wrong",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["epic window"]
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "could",
            "note": "none yet;  ask Owen first when a view looks stuck"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["spell-app window"],
            "note": "`reload-view [--review]`"
          },
          "runs": "`scripts/window.mjs reload-view` -> the bridge's `reload-view` -> `DocView.rebuild()`",
          "notes": "A new iframe at the page in view, where the view's reload button only navigates the old one.  Pages stuck on placeholders were the 6-connection cap, fixed by websocket live reload (worktree `docs-sidebar`), not this.",
          "target": "built:  `epic window reload` (worktree `docs-sidebar`, 2026-10-06)"
        },
        {
          "op": "Give a window a look (a colour scheme)",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["epic window"]
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["/epic"],
            "note": "`/epic color <look>`;  `/epic <name> -<look>` and `/isolate <name> -<look>` pass `open --color`"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["spell-app window"],
            "note": "`color [<look>]`"
          },
          "runs": "`scripts/window.mjs color <look>` -> writes the window's `.code-workspace` settings (`withLook()`)",
          "notes": "Tomorrow Night Blue's look in one of 12 hues;  VS Code applies it at once, no reload, extensions untouched (Q11 of `windows-and-review`).",
          "target": "built:  `epic window color` (epic `windows-and-review` P5, 2026-10-06)"
        },
        {
          "op": "Title and tint the window a session stays in",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["epic window"]
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["/isolate", "/epic", "/unpark"],
            "note": "`stay <name>` when Owen picks \"Stay in this window\";  `stay --end` at `/isolate done`"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["spell-app window"],
            "note": "`stay <name> | --end`"
          },
          "runs": "`scripts/window.mjs stay` -> `withStay()` / `withoutStay()` on the window's `.code-workspace`",
          "notes": "Titled `⎇ <name>`, title bar tinted;  what it replaced kept in `spell.stay`, put back by `--end`.",
          "target": "built:  `epic window stay` (epic `windows-and-review` P5, 2026-10-06)"
        },
        {
          "op": "Write missing package window files",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["epic window"]
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "could",
            "note": "none uses it;  AGENTS.md says run it by hand"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["spell-app window"],
            "note": "`init`"
          },
          "runs": "`scripts/window.mjs init`",
          "notes": "Never overwrites:  themes are Owen's.  Writes them in the windows folder (`epic config windowsFolder`).",
          "target": "(R2) built:  `epic window init`;  yarn `window:init` aliases it"
        },
        {
          "op": "Move the window files out of the repo, once",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["epic window"],
            "note": "`move [--dry-run]`:  `workspaces/` to the content folder's `windows/`, each folder path rewritten"
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "no"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "no"
          },
          "runs": "`src/window.mjs move` (spell-epic)",
