            "mark": "other",
            "names": ["spell-app lsp:scopes"],
            "note": "`--compile <projectId...>`, then writes scope packs"
          },
          "runs": "`CLI.compileCommand` -> `SpellProject.compile()`;  writes `<Project>.compiled.js`, `<Project>.declarations.json` and each other target's output (`project.json` `targets`, or `--target <name>` this run;  `SP.TARGETS`)",
          "notes": "VS Code:  the language server compiles after each clean save.  The app compiles too.",
          "target": "stays:  spell-language command `spell compile`"
        },
        {
          "op": "Print a project's compiled javascript without writing it",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["spell compile"],
            "note": "`--stdout`;  a `.spell` file prints by default"
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "could"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "could"
          },
          "runs": "`SpellProject.compile(scope, { save: false })`",
          "notes": "VS Code:  Show Compiled JavaScript (`spell.showCompiled`).  `spell describe --compiled` for one thing.",
          "target": "stays:  spell-language command `spell compile --stdout`"
        },
        {
          "op": "Recompile the projects a project imports",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["spell compile"],
            "note": "`--force`"
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "could"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "could"
          },
          "runs": "`spell compile --force`",
          "notes": "Without it, an imported project's stale `.compiled.js` is used as is.",
          "target": "stays:  spell-language command `spell compile --force`"
        },
        {
          "op": "Compile only the projects whose build is missing or out of date",
          "cli": {
            "mark": "same",
            "names": ["spell compile"],
            "note": "`--stale`, e.g. `spell compile --stale --all @examples @library`"
          },
          "skill": {
            "mark": "could"
          },
          "yarn": {
            "mark": "could"
          },
          "runs": "`spell compile --stale` -> `CLI.staleBecause()`:  a built file missing, or one of the project's files, its `project.json`, an import's declarations or spell's compiler newer than its build;  the same for what it imports (epic `people-and-orgs` P11)",
          "notes": "The page server runs it for `@examples` and `@library` when it starts (`ProjectBuild`, in the app's route module);  the app's API compiles a project whose built file is missing before serving it.",
          "target": "stays:  spell-language command `spell compile --stale`"
        },
        {
          "op": "Write a project's scope pack (`<Project>.scopes.js`)",
